# Astro: the boot-success milestone (docs/02 §5.1, docs/05 §4, AD-011).
# Internal service whose dependencies DEFINE "this boot is good":
#   base set (M1) = astrod healthy + data-mount done.
# Rollback-participating app services (docs/08 §5) add themselves here as
# depends-on at image assembly (M4). rauc-mark-good gains
# "depends-on: boot-success" at M2 — if this milestone is never reached,
# the bootloader's attempt counters fall back to the other slot.
#
# before login.target (M3 phase 2): astrod now depends-on dbus-daemon,
# which itself is only "before: login.target" — without the same ordering
# here, dinit reached login (and released the console) while astrod was
# still coming up, so the "[  OK  ] boot-success" line never hit serial
# (the milestone WAS reached — rauc-mark-good ran — but invisibly, which
# broke the boot-smoke assertion and, more importantly, put the login
# prompt ahead of the good-boot decision). Ordering only: on a broken
# slot the milestone fails and login proceeds; the watchdog handles the
# rest (AD-011).
before: login.target

type = internal
depends-on: astrod
depends-on: data-mount
